 0. PATH RECONCILIATION (no silent drift)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt names the output `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Admin/**`.
That directory is NOT a compiled source root in this repo. `project.yml` compiles
the app target from `Sources/**` plus a fixed set of `TeslaSync/<group>` dirs
(widget-primitives, dashboard-widgets, feature-views, misc-surfaces,
shared-surfaces). EVERY sibling admin page lives in `Sources/Features/Admin/`
(APIKeysPage, AuditLogPage, DiskForecastPage, TeslaOrdersPage, …). To produce a
file that actually builds + integrates (not dead code), the page was authored at
`Sources/Features/Admin/`, matching sibling precedent. swiftlint + placeholder
scans were run against the real path. This is the honest mapping of the prompt's
idealized path onto the actual repo layout.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 1. WEB SOURCE ANALYSIS + COMPOSITION (no predecessor bypass)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
web/src/features/admin/pages/SystemPage.tsx is a thin PageContainer:
  PageContainer(title = t('system.page.title','System budgets'),
                subtitle = t('system.page.subtitle','Operator dashboard …'))
    > FadeIn > Stack(gap-6)
        > <RateLimitStatusPanel />
        > <QueueStatusPanel />
The page holds NO data of its own — each panel owns its own polling hook.

Manifest record `page:admin/System`: kind=page, requiredCount=2,
strings=[system.page.subtitle, system.page.title], 0 dataSources / 0 panels /
0 charts / 0 maps. The two panels are admin-feature-local child components that
the manifest did not extract as part of this page unit.

The two panels are ALREADY SHIPPED as P4 Apple feature-views (predecessors):
  TeslaSync/feature-views/RateLimitStatusPanel.swift   (P4 0038) — public View(model: RateLimitModel)
  TeslaSync/feature-views/QueueStatusPanel.swift       (P4 0037) — public View(model: QueueStatusModel)
Following the sibling precedent (TeslaOrdersPage composes the shipped
ActiveOrdersSection), SystemPage COMPOSES the two shipped panels rather than
re-implementing them (= no predecessor bypass, no scope narrowing). Each panel
already renders all of its own loading / error / empty / populated states + the
stale/offline freshness overlays, and resolves its own strings from its own
.strings table.

NOTE on the per-worker jobs drawer: web QueueStatusPanel embeds <QueueJobDrawer>.
The Apple QueueStatusPanel deliberately externalizes that via an `onOpenWorker`
callback, and the Apple QueueJobDrawer (TeslaSync/modals-dialogs/QueueJobDrawer)
is a SEPARATE surface that is NOT compiled into the app target (modals-dialogs is
absent from project.yml sources). It is therefore out of this page's buildable
scope; the panel's default no-op `onOpenWorker` is used, exactly as the panel's
own contract documents. The page reproduces every region of SystemPage.tsx
itself (title + subtitle + the two panels).

